.page-header
  %h2 Bluesky Sync Settings

= comfy_form_with model: @config, scope: :bluesky_sync_config, url: comfy_admin_bluesky_sync_config_path, method: :patch do |form|

  = form.text_field :handle,
                    label: "Handle (full handle, e.g. sexyverse.bsky.social — not the bare username)"

  = form.password_field :app_password,
                        label: "App password (Bluesky › Settings › App Passwords — keep the hyphens)",
                        help: @config.app_password.present? ? "A password is already saved. Leave blank to keep it." : "No password saved yet.",
                        autocomplete: "new-password"

  = form.text_field :service_host,
                    label: "Service host (leave as https://bsky.social unless using a custom PDS)"

  = form.text_area :lead,
                   label: "Teaser lead — first line above the title + link (all posts)",
                   style: "field-sizing: content;"

  = form.text_area :lead_shite,
                   label: "Teaser lead — for 'Shite Advice' posts (falls back to the default lead if blank)",
                   style: "field-sizing: content;"

  = form.form_actions do
    = submit_tag "Save", class: "btn btn-primary ml-sm-1"

%hr
%p.text-muted.small
  Posts are mirrored to Bluesky as a teaser (lead + title + link) with a link card,
  from the "Sync to Bluesky" button on each post. Bluesky's 300-character cap can't
  hold a full post, so the card links back to the blog.
